## Junior Project Manager - Innovation and Data

Industrial holdings of Lugano (AIL) SA — open position in Lugano/Muzzano (TI).

AIL SA Casella postale 6901 Lugano Centre Via Industria 2 6933 Muzzano Tel. 058 470 70 www.ail.ch
• info@ail.ch Who we are: We are a dynamic company in the energy sector and in the supply of drinking water, evolving and with a strong focus on innovation and development of people. To strengthen, continue to develop and manage the activities of AIL:LAB, our laboratory of innovation and organizational transformation, we look for a motivated person for the role of Junior Project Manager - Innovation and Data 80%-100% Your impact: Referring directly to the Director of the People and Future area, in this role you will contribute to the operation and growth of AIL:LAB, supporting the management and realization of projects of innovation, digitization and valorisation of data, while promoting organizational change. You will be an operational and technical-functional reference point for coordinating activities, collecting and structuring requirements and developing digital and data-driven solutions, working closely with technical and corporate interlocutors. You will also contribute to the dissemination of innovation and continuous improvement within the Company. What you will do concretely:
• you will support the management and implementation of projects and initiatives promoted by AIL:LAB, with particular attention to aspects related to technological innovation, data and automation;
• you will collect the needs of different corporate units and contribute to transducing them into functional and technical requirements, coordinating activities and stakeholders involved;
• you will contribute to the design and development of data collection, integration, processing and enhancement solutions;
• you will perform analysis, dashboards and reporting tools, contributing to the definition of KPIs and information models;
• you will use SQL, Python or other scripting tools for data processing and analysis;
• you will help to structure data and digital solutions so that they can be used in innovative projects and in artificial intelligence-based use cases;
• you will prepare the project documentation and collaborate with the communication, workshops and change management necessary to foster the adoption of the developed solutions. Who are you?
• you have a university education in Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Management Engineering with Digital Guidance/Date or equivalent training;
• any specializations in Data Analytics, Data Engineering, Innovation or related areas constitute preferential title;
• you have an excellent knowledge of the Italian language and a good knowledge of English;
• you can understand corporate needs and translate them into solutions, working effectively with both technical and non-technical interlocutors;
• you have experience or solid knowledge in data, relational databases and SQL;
• know Business Intelligence, Data Visualization and Data Engineering tools;
• you have interest and experience in using cloud platforms and data platform;
• preferably you have knowledge of Microsoft Azure, Databriks, MS Fabric or assimilar technologies, as well as Python and data integration tools;
• you are a curious, analytical, organized and collaborative person, with problem solving, autonomy and interest in innovation and continuous improvement;
• you have Swiss citizenship or a residence permit. What we offer:
• a collaborative working environment, with ample space to bring ideas and innovation;
• the possibility of growing professionally, acquiring new skills and responsibilities;
• flexibility and support to reconcile professional and personal life;
• possibility of further training and continuing training;
• Contractual conditions, insurance and social security. Attachment documents:
• motivational letter;
• complete dossier of curriculum vitae, diplomas and work certificates;
• copy of the identity document. At a later date, an excerpt from the execution and bankruptcy office will be required and an updated judicial checkout with a maximum validity of 3 months. End of the competition: Friday 4 September 2026.

 Application deadline:* 2026-09-05

Sector: Energy / Public Services

Sede: Via Industria 2, 6933 Muzzano (Lugano), TI, Switzerland

[Official note (PDF)](https://www.ail.ch/downloadJobPosition?uuid=ff2c7c55-9b41-4ea6-a9db-b1769b8ad1a1)

